From 91b9daaa8cdba18375f0afe14c725ff63a3e19cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oussama Benjelloun <benje.oussama@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:16:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] HIP: address independent review findings

- An explicit hip_gfx* feature now wins over HL_HIP_ARCH (the env var is
  consulted only when no arch feature is set), so Module/JIT/generator
  caches keyed on the target string stay correct.
- gpu_object_lifetime_tracker knows hipMalloc/hipFree.
- Document that in-kernel assertions trap (s_trap) and that ROCm reports
  this through the queue error callback rather than a recoverable error.
- halide_hip_device_release restores the caller's current device.
- Host arch autodetect is silent when no HIP library/device is present.
- f64 atomic add is supported on every arch (CAS-expanded where needed).
- correctness_hip_code_object decodes the AMDGPU metadata msgpack and
  asserts the exact kernarg layout, and rejects any relocation entry.
- IRPrinter/StmtToHTML no longer print the binary code object as text;
  CodeGen_C emits HalideRuntimeHIP.h; DeviceAPI::HIP appended at the end
  of the enum; link failures are user errors with lld's diagnostics;
  Makefile/xcframework/docs consistency fixes.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
